    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d323">

                <pb facs="0445" n="434" xml:id="pg434"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">211.68/159</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Greece</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Shantz</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1887</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Athens</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-09-30">September 30, 1937</date>.<lb/>[Received October
                        19.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In reference to the Department’s telegram
                    No. 36 of September 29, 1937, I have the honor to report that I have today
                    addressed a Note<anchor n="23" xml:id="d323-f1"/> to His Excellency John
                    Metaxas, President of the Council and Minister for Foreign Affairs, formally
                    withdrawing the notice of abrogation of the Extradition Treaty of May 6, 1931,
                    between the United States and Greece, which was delivered to the Greek
                    Government on November 6, 1933,<anchor n="24" xml:id="d323-f2"/> pursuant to the
                    Department’s telegraphic instruction No. 55 of November 4, 1933.<anchor n="23"
                        xml:id="d323-f3"/></p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Harold Shantz</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
